Roles {#role}
=====================

A <dfn>Role</dfn> is a collection of [=Social Agents=],
internal to the context of the [=Social Agent=] defining the Role.

<table class="classinfo data" align="left" id="classRole">
  <colgroup></colgroup>
  <colgroup></colgroup>
  <colgroup></colgroup>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Property</th>
      <th>Range</th>
      <th>Description</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td>hasMember</td>
      <td>[SocialAgent](#classSocialAgent)</td>
      <td>[=Social Agent=] assigned as a member to the [=Role=]</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<figure>
  <figcaption>[=Role=] with member Bob at https://alice.example/roles/a7c349e2 -
  <a href="snippets/alice.example/a7c349e2.ttl">View</a>
</figcaption>
  <pre class=include-code>
  path: snippets/alice.example/a7c349e2.ttl
  highlight: turtle
  </pre>
</figure>

When [=Authorization Agent=] generates [=Data Grants=] from a [=Data Authorization=] it
* MUST generate a [=Data Grant=] for each member of that [=Role=] as `dataOwner` if a [=Role=] is used as `dataOwner`.
* MUST generate a [=Data Grant=] for each member of that [=Role=] as `grantee` if a [=Role=] is used as `grantee`.
* MUST generate a [=Data Grant=] for the cartesian product of the two [=Roles=], with each member as corresponding `dataOwner` or `grantee` if a [=Role=] is used as both `dataOwner` and `grantee`.

When a [=Role=] is modified, [=Authorization Agent=] managing it
* MUST generate corresponding [=Data Grants=], when a member is added to the [=Role=]
* MUST revoke corresponding [=Data Grants=], when a member is removed from the [=Role=]
* MUST revoke [=Data Authorizations=] where the role was used as a `dataOwner` or a `grantee`, when the [=Role=] is deleted.

Note: When [=Data Authorization=] is revoked, [=Data Grants=] that are derrived because of it also must be revoked.

## Role Registry ## {#datamodel-role-registry}

A <dfn>Role Registry</dfn> contains all the [=Roles=] defined by the [=Social Agent=] who owns the [=Role Registry=]

<table class="classinfo data" align="left" id="classRoleRegistry">
